# Color Formats: Hex & RGB 🔴🟢🔵

CSS supports multiple color notations:

## 1. Hexadecimal (`#RRGGBB`):
Uses base-16 (0-9, A-F) representing Red, Green, and Blue channels:
```css_not
.box {
  background-color: #3b82f6; /* Blue */
  color: #ffffff;            /* White */
}
```
With alpha transparency: `#3b82f680` (80 in hex = ~50% opacity).

## 2. RGB & RGBA:
```css_not
/* rgb(red, green, blue) - values from 0 to 255 */
.box {
  background-color: rgb(59, 130, 246);

  /* Modern CSS Syntax with alpha slash: */
  background-color: rgb(59 130 246 / 0.5); /* 50% opacity */
}
```

# HSL: Designed for Humans 💡

**HSL** stands for **H**ue, **S**aturation, and **L**ightness. It is far more intuitive to modify programmatically than Hex or RGB:

```css_not
/* hsl(hue [0-360], saturation [0-100%], lightness [0-100%]) */
.brand {
  background-color: hsl(217, 91%, 60%);
}
```

- **Hue (0-360°):** Position on the color wheel (0° Red, 120° Green, 240° Blue).
- **Saturation (0-100%):** 0% is pure gray, 100% is vibrant full color.
- **Lightness (0-100%):** 0% is pitch black, 50% is normal, 100% is pure white.

> 🎯 **Pro Tip:** Need a hover effect? Just change lightness from 60% to 50%!

# Modern Color Space: OKLCH 🚀

Modern browsers support `oklch()`. Unlike RGB and HSL, OKLCH is **perceptually uniform**: two colors with the same lightness value look equally bright to the human eye across all hues!

```css_not
/* oklch(Lightness [0-1], Chroma [0-0.4], Hue [0-360]) */
.badge-blue {
  background-color: oklch(0.65 0.20 250);
}

.badge-yellow {
  /* Exactly the same perceived brightness as the blue badge above! */
  background-color: oklch(0.65 0.20 95);
}
```

# The `currentColor` Keyword 🪄

`currentColor` is a built-in variable that matches the computed value of the element's `color` property!

```css_not
.button {
  color: #2563eb;
  border: 2px solid currentColor; /* Automatically uses #2563eb! */
}

.button svg {
  fill: currentColor; /* SVG icon automatically matches text color! */
}

/* On hover, changing color changes the border and SVG icon simultaneously! */
.button:hover {
  color: #1d4ed8;
}
```

# Linear Gradients (`linear-gradient`) 🌈

Linear gradients create smooth transitions between two or more colors along a straight line:

```css_not
/* Syntax: linear-gradient([direction/angle], color1, color2, ...) */
.gradient-card {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #3b82f6, #8b5cf6);
}

/* Direction keywords */
.to-right {
  background: linear-gradient(to right, #ec4899, #f43f5e);
}
```

## Directions:
- Degrees: `0deg` (up), `90deg` (right), `180deg` (down), `270deg` (left).
- Keywords: `to top`, `to right`, `to bottom`, `to top right`.

# Multi-Stop & Hard-Stop Gradients 🎨

Gradients can transition across multiple colors and custom stop positions:

```css_not
/* Multi-color rainbow gradient */
.rainbow {
  background: linear-gradient(to right, #f43f5e, #f59e0b, #10b981, #3b82f6);
}

/* Hard color stop (creates sharp dual-colored split bar!) */
.split-banner {
  background: linear-gradient(to right, #3b82f6 50%, #10b981 50%);
}
```

# Radial Gradients (`radial-gradient`) ☀️

Radial gradients radiate outward from an origin point:

```css_not
/* Syntax: radial-gradient([shape] at [position], color1, color2) */
.glowing-orb {
  background: radial-gradient(circle at center, #60a5fa, #1e3a8a);
}

/* Off-center spotlight effect */
.spotlight {
  background: radial-gradient(ellipse at top right, rgba(255,255,255,0.3), #0f172a);
}
```

# Background Images (`background-image`) 🖼️

Attach an image to the background of an element:

```css_not
.hero-section {
  background-image: url('images/hero-bg.jpg');
  background-repeat: no-repeat;
  background-position: center center;
  background-size: cover;
}
```

## Core Properties:
- `background-repeat`: `no-repeat`, `repeat`, `repeat-x`, `repeat-y`.
- `background-position`: `center`, `top left`, `50% 50%`, `10px 20px`.

# Background Attachment (`background-attachment`) 🧲

Controls how background images react to page scrolling:

```css_not
.parallax-banner {
  background-image: url('mountains.jpg');
  background-size: cover;
  background-position: center;
  background-attachment: fixed; /* Fixed relative to viewport! */
}
```

- `scroll` *(Default)*: Background scrolls along with the page content.
- `fixed`: Background stays fixed in the viewport while the content scrolls over it (simple parallax effect!).

# Layering Multiple Backgrounds 🥞

CSS allows you to apply multiple comma-separated backgrounds to a single element. The first background listed is rendered on top!

```css_not
/* Layer a semi-transparent gradient on top of a photographic image */
.hero {
  background: 
    linear-gradient(rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.8), rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.8)),
    url('hero-photo.jpg') center/cover no-repeat;
  color: #ffffff;
}
```

This guarantees text readability over bright background photographs!

# Gradient Text with `background-clip: text` ✨

You can clip a gradient background directly into letterforms:

```css_not
.gradient-headline {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #3b82f6, #ec4899);
  -webkit-background-clip: text;
  background-clip: text;
  color: transparent; /* Makes text fill transparent so gradient shines through! */
  font-size: 3rem;
  font-weight: 800;
}
```

# Modern UI: Glassmorphism with `backdrop-filter` 🪟

Create sleek frosted-glass effects:

```css_not
.glass-navbar {
  position: fixed;
  top: 0;
  width: 100%;
  background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7); /* Semi-transparent */
  backdrop-filter: blur(12px);                /* Blurs content behind the navbar! */
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.3);
}
```

# The `background` Shorthand Property 🖌️

Combine all background properties into a single rule:

```css_not
/* Syntax: background: [color] [image] [position]/[size] [repeat] [attachment] */
.hero {
  background: #0f172a url('stars.png') center/cover no-repeat fixed;
}
```

> ⚠️ **Shorthand Note:** The `size` MUST follow `position` separated by a forward slash `/` (e.g. `center/cover`).

# Real-World Component: Hero Card 🌟

```html_not
<div class="hero-card">
  <span class="badge">New Release</span>
  <h2>Build Without Boundaries</h2>
  <p>Ship modern software with full-stack speed and elegance.</p>
</div>
```

```css_not
.hero-card {
  padding: 48px;
  border-radius: 24px;
  background: 
    radial-gradient(circle at 100% 0%, rgba(236, 72, 153, 0.2), transparent 40%),
    linear-gradient(135deg, #0f172a, #1e293b);
  color: #f8fafc;
  box-shadow: 0 20px 25px -5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
}
```
